        "description": "For millennia, humans have created art with the power to shock, disturb and offend. But what makes an artwork truly dangerous? And should it ever be censored? From Hitler’s paintings to the racist caricatures of Jim Crow America, Daisy Dixon takes Jon Bauckham on a tour of history’s most depraved art, revealing both its capacity for cruelty and its use as a tool of oppression. Please note, this episode does contain explicit discussions of themes including sexual violence and racism. Listener discretion is advised. ----- GO BEYOND THE PODCAST Discover more about slave trader Edward Colston in this episode featuring historian Richard Stone: https://bit.ly/4rd19W8 ----- GET MORE WITH MEMBERSHIP Become a HistoryExtra podcast member and unlock access to The Full Story podcast, plus enjoy ad-free listening, early access to other podcast episodes, and a member-exclusive newsletter. Find out more and sign up here: ⁠https://historyextra.supportingcast.fm⁠ ----- EXPLORE MORE For more fascinating stories from the past, head to HistoryExtra, the home of ‘History’s Greatest’ podcasts. Find out more at ⁠⁠⁠historyextra.com/podcast⁠⁠⁠. ----- GET IN TOUCH We'd love to know what you think about the podcast, so leave us a review and let us know the topics you think we should be covering. Or, follow us on ⁠Facebook⁠, ⁠X⁠, ⁠Instagram⁠ or ⁠YouTube⁠ to keep in touch. Learn more about your ad choices. Visit podcastchoices.com/adchoices",
